I have this story about one time,

00:06:49.859 --> 00:06:52.140
I guess I was a freshman in college,

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.510
I met this girl, she was
older, she was a junior,

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.490
and we'd talk in the bar and we'd hang out

00:06:56.490 --> 00:07:00.062
for a little while and
one night, I'm drunk,

00:07:00.062 --> 00:07:01.770
and she's living on the first floor

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.750
of this apartment
building, and I go outside

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:05.550
and I'm singing Billy Joel songs.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.190
- [Kelly] You're John Cusack!
- Outside her window.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:08.023
- [Kelly] Just outside the window?

00:07:08.023 --> 00:07:09.000
- Yeah, outside her window.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.950
She came out and she
laughed, and she led me in

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:11.783
and we had a beer.

00:07:11.783 --> 00:07:12.616
I'll leave it at that.

00:07:12.616 --> 00:07:13.693
Yeah, so we had a beer.

00:07:13.693 --> 00:07:14.590
(Darius and audience laughing)

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:15.423
- They had a beer.

00:07:15.423 --> 00:07:16.560
- Yeah, we had a beer.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:17.940
- Congratulations on that beer.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.230
- That was good.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.215
- I would work that angle too
if I had that kind of voice.

00:07:21.215 --> 00:07:23.400
I'd be like, "Yes, ladies!"

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.860
Did you, a lot of us too,
I always run into musicians

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:27.360
and I feel like we all
grew up singing in church.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.353
Did you grow up singing in church?

00:07:28.353 --> 00:07:29.186
- Absolutely.
- Yeah, me too.

00:07:29.186 --> 00:07:30.438
- Amazing Grace was, you know,

00:07:30.438 --> 00:07:33.818
♪ Amazing grace ♪

00:07:33.818 --> 00:07:36.494
♪ How sweet the sound ♪

00:07:36.494 --> 00:07:41.052
♪ That saved a wretch like me ♪

00:07:41.052 --> 00:07:41.968
That was my song!

00:07:41.968 --> 00:07:43.341
- Yes!

00:07:43.341 --> 00:07:44.277
- [Darius] I love that song.

00:07:44.277 --> 00:07:45.974
- We all have a go-to.

00:07:45.974 --> 00:07:47.489
Mine was His Eye Is On The Sparrow.

00:07:47.489 --> 00:07:48.322
- [Darius] Oh, absolutely!

00:07:48.322 --> 00:07:49.155
- I love Amazing Grace, but
His Eye Is On The Sparrow,

00:07:49.155 --> 00:07:50.501
I think 'cause I saw Sister
Act when I was a little kid,

00:07:50.501 --> 00:07:53.266
and I was like, "I wanna be Lauryn Hill!"

00:07:53.266 --> 00:07:55.050
I was like, yeah, I loved them.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:55.883
I thought it was so good.

00:07:55.883 --> 00:07:57.420
But those songs, I feel like,

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.220
I feel like I sing differently

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.170
because I have that
background, you almost,

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.330
you know there's a bigger
purpose for all of us

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.470
and it's bigger than you.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:07.020
And when that's instilled
in you at such a young age,

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:09.390
I think spiritual people sing differently.

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:10.223
- I agree.

00:08:10.223 --> 00:08:11.910
- [Kelly] Yeah, whatever your
belief is, I just mean like,

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.370
I feel like if you believe
in something bigger than you,

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:17.640
and outside of yourself,
it's a different sound

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:18.473
that comes from you.
- [Darius] I agree.

00:08:18.473 --> 00:08:20.070
I think you sing from your soul.

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:20.903
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:20.903 --> 00:08:22.230
- You sing from as far in
the depths of your soul

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.063
as you can and I think

00:08:23.063 --> 00:08:24.130
that creates something really special.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.320
- [Kelly] Yeah, it's
almost like you're able

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:27.300
to put your ego aside, 'cause
we're told at a very young age

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.650
like, it's not for you, it's for the Lord.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.711
It's not for you, it's
for something bigger.

00:08:30.711 --> 00:08:31.544
- [Darius] Exactly.

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:33.000
- I love that you just sang on my show.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.650
I was like, "alright, alright!"

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:36.600
I heard that, too, I love Ed Sheeran,

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:37.890
I got to work with him on The Voice,

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:39.420
and you did a song with him, right?

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:40.491
- We did, I did.

00:08:40.491 --> 00:08:44.340
I went to, I've known Ed for
years and I went to England

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.260
to write with him and
when I first sat down,

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:47.430
we were writing the song, and he asks me

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:49.140
who my first love was.

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:51.720
And I said it was my fifth
grade girlfriend, Sarah.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.370
And he asked me these million questions

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:54.757
and then at the end of
the session, he's like,

00:08:54.757 --> 00:08:55.710
"Hey, I got one more song,

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.120
let's write the song about Sarah."

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.200
And I said, you want to write a song

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.160
about my fifth grade girlfriend?

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:01.110
I haven't talked to her in 45 years!

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:01.950
And you wanna talk-

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:03.150
and we wrote a song called Sarah

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.170
about my fifth grade girlfriend.

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:06.570
- You wanna know why I think
that's such a great idea?

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.917
We always, I feel like
adults always say like,

00:09:08.917 --> 00:09:10.320
"Oh, they're children,
what do they know of love?"

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.153
Or, "What do they know of this?"

00:09:11.153 --> 00:09:14.250
And I'm like, I think,
children, they're not jaded yet.

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:15.083
- Oh, exactly.

00:09:15.083 --> 00:09:16.800
- I think that kids feel everything.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:19.050
I never tell my kids when they come home,

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:20.707
they're 7 and 9, but
they already are like,

00:09:20.707 --> 00:09:21.540
"Oh, I love him."

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.670
And I'm like, "I truly
believe you probably do

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:24.780
with your whole heart!"

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:26.686
I'm like, you know, "You
probably gonna change your mind,

00:09:26.686 --> 00:09:29.910
but like, I'm just gonna let you know."

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:32.460
But yeah, I just think
it's such a pure thing

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:35.790
and there's no other
experience jading that.

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:36.623
- Yes, I agree.

00:09:36.623 --> 00:09:38.010
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- I agree.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:38.843
I love the song.

00:09:38.843 --> 00:09:39.750
Ed's such a great songwriter.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.040
- [Kelly] I have to ask you this too

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.040
because this album art is beautiful.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:44.873
This your momma?

00:09:44.873 --> 00:09:45.706
- That's my mom.

00:09:45.706 --> 00:09:46.539
- [Kelly] Oh my god, what was the idea,

00:09:46.539 --> 00:09:48.660
why did you end up using this picture?

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:50.850
- [Darius] Well, that's her nursing school

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:53.370
graduation picture, she
was 24 in that picture

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:56.370
and all of our family has
that picture up on their wall.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.380
And, you know, my mom
was so special to me.

00:09:58.380 --> 00:09:59.520
She was such a great human being.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.250
She was, like I said, she
was my biggest supporter,

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:03.581
my biggest fan.

00:10:03.581 --> 00:10:06.210
When I decided to name
the record Carolyn's Boy,

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:07.710
I knew it was gonna be that picture.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:08.790
- [Kelly] Yeah?
- It's a great picture.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:09.623
- I love that.

00:10:09.623 --> 00:10:11.730
I'm like that when I write
too, I have imagery going,

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:13.500
I have to like almost
paint a picture in my head

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.333
while I'm doing it.

00:10:14.333 --> 00:10:15.300
- [Darius] Oh, me too.
- Yeah.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.317
- [Darius] Every song I write,
there's a video in my head.

00:10:17.317 --> 00:10:18.150
- [Kelly] Me too!
- Yeah.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.558
- [Kelly] Okay I thought I was weird.

00:10:19.558 --> 00:10:20.391
- You are, but-

00:10:20.391 --> 00:10:21.224
- Yeah!

00:10:21.224 --> 00:10:22.057
(Darius and audience laughing)

00:10:22.057 --> 00:10:23.970
You are, but I am too.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.590
What do you feel like the best lesson,

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:26.880
other than her being so supportive,

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:28.230
I imagine you're like that with your kids

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.570
because you were taught
that from a young age,

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:32.130
but what do you think the biggest lesson

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:33.030
you got from her was?

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:34.110
- [Darius] Oh, believe in yourself.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.006
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:35.006 --> 00:10:36.570
- 'Cause we grew up in a
really poor neighborhood

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.850
with not much and, you
know, there was no reason

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:41.100
for me to believe that I was
gonna be here and make it

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:42.960
but she always instilled
in me, believe in yourself,

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:44.212
you can do whatever you want.

00:10:44.212 --> 00:10:47.031
I instill that in my
kids and I believe it.

00:10:47.031 --> 00:10:48.193
- That's incredible.

00:10:48.193 --> 00:10:50.130
'Cause not all parents do that,

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:51.484
you know what I'm saying?
- [Darius] Definitely not.

00:10:51.484 --> 00:10:52.317
I know.

00:10:52.317 --> 00:10:53.760
When I was a kid, she instilled in us

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.980
that you help people, not
people that are less fortunate,

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:57.420
you help people that need help.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:59.580
I tell the story about my
brother, I guess I was 10.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:01.050
Probably not 10, I was probably 7 or 8,

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:04.140
my brother was 14 and we had this couple

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.010
that lived in our neighborhood

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.390
and the husband was in the navy.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:07.223
- Uh huh.

00:11:07.223 --> 00:11:08.490
- [Darius] And so, he
went away on the ship,

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:11.520
and the yard was growing
up and my brother went over

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.280
and cut her grass, and she gave him $10.

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.440
And he came home bragging
about the $10 he got,

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.937
and my mom whooped his butt and told him,

00:11:18.937 --> 00:11:21.960
"You take that $10 back down
and you give it back to her

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.370
because we don't help people for money,

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.690
we help people to help people."

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:25.800
And that was just something
she instilled in us.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:27.758
- [Kelly] Oh wow!
- Yeah.

00:11:27.758 --> 00:11:30.978
- You got a great mom!

00:11:30.978 --> 00:11:31.811
Wow.

00:11:31.811 --> 00:11:32.809
Very lucky.

00:11:32.809 --> 00:11:34.110
Well, we have a little surprise for you

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:35.640
and I was very excited
to be able to do this.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:36.473
- [Darius] Do you?
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:11:36.473 --> 00:11:37.800
You don't know, he really
doesn't know about it.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.691
This is not TV, this is real.

00:11:39.691 --> 00:11:43.290
For your many, many charitable
efforts over the years

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:45.390
and for helping those who need help,

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:49.035
CMA is actually honoring you
as Humanitarian of the Year.

00:11:49.035 --> 00:11:49.868
- Wow!

00:11:49.868 --> 00:11:51.359
- You got your trophy and everything!

00:11:51.359 --> 00:11:52.192
- Oh my goodness!

00:11:52.192 --> 00:11:54.123
(audience cheering)

00:11:54.123 --> 00:11:55.206
Wow!

00:11:55.206 --> 00:11:56.995
- I'm so excited!
- That's awesome!

00:11:56.995 --> 00:11:57.828
Wow.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:11:59.573
Wow!

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:02.190
I really did not know that!

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:03.658
- I know!

00:12:03.658 --> 00:12:05.304
I was like, "No, he really doesn't know!"

00:12:05.304 --> 00:12:06.240
- I did not know that.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.800
- Alright, well, let's do another break.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:10.410
Darius' latest album is
called Carolyn's Boy,

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.970
it's out right now,
y'all gotta check it out

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:14.970
and he's also designed
his own line of NFL gear

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.760
which is super cool, rad,
which is available in stores

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:19.733
and online, so y'all gotta check that out.

